  },
  "collection": {
    "command": "PYTHONPATH=src PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m pytest --collect-only -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/",
    "cwd": "the interlock checkout root",
    "python": "3.12.3",
    "pytest": "9.1.1",
    "note": "The WHOLE suite is collected once and split by path afterwards. Collecting each subsystem in its own pytest run is not the same measurement: conftest hooks and import order differ between a whole-tree run and a single-directory one, so a per-subsystem run can collect a different set and nothing in the resulting files would say so. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE and -p no:cacheprovider keep the run from writing into the interlock checkout, which is read-only reference material here."
  },
